{
  "uid": "cafaye-stack-overview",
  "title": "cafaye — local stack",
  "description": "The four stores and the collector, from a self-hoster's first question: 'what does this look like when it breaks'. Every panel here is a liveness signal for a component of the stack that ships by default, so the first five minutes after `bin/dev up` answer themselves.",
  "tags": [
    "cafaye",
    "stack"
  ],
  "timezone": "utc",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 1,
  "editable": false,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "refresh": "10s",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "timepicker": {},
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "The stack, on by default",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "Observability is **on by default and worked on in dev** (PLAN.md §7b). You did not have to install anything: `bin/dev up` brought up the collector and the four stores behind it, and a service with nothing configured exports into them because `<SERVICE>_OTEL_ENDPOINT` defaults to the collector that ships with this stack.\n\n**Telemetry is never in anyone's readiness path.** Kill the collector and every service here keeps serving — you lose spans, not traffic. `tests/no_telemetry_in_readiness.sh` in `kit` proves exactly that, on every commit.\n\n**Grafana, Loki, Tempo and Mimir are AGPL-3.0 and ship unmodified.** Configuration is mounted read-only over the stock images; nothing is forked, patched or rebranded. AGPL attaches to the Grafana *server*, not to the applications it observes, so this is compatible with cafaye being MIT/Apache.\n\n**To bring your own backend**, set `<SERVICE>_OTEL_ENDPOINT` in your service to your Datadog / Honeycomb / Grafana Cloud OTLP endpoint and this stack goes quiet for that service. That is a supported deployment, not a degraded mode. **To turn telemetry off**, unset the variable: the exporter becomes a genuine no-op — no queue, no retry loop, no warning per request, no dial at boot."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "row",
      "title": "Collector — the chokepoint",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 1,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 5
      },
      "collapsed": false,
      "panels": []
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Spans accepted / s",
      "description": "What the redaction allowlist let through. Everything else was stripped before an exporter saw it, which is why this number is the honest measure of what telemetry is being collected.",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "mimir",
        "uid": "mimir"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 5,
        "w": 6,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 6
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "refId": "A",
          "expr": "sum(rate(cafaye_calls_total[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "spans/s",
          "datasource": {
            "type": "prometheus",
            "uid": "mimir"
          }
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ],
          "fields": "",
          "values": false
        },
        "colorMode": "none",
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps",
          "decimals": 2
        },
        "overrides": []
      }
    },
    {
